{
 "about": "The app's components for `tools/gate.py` (the owner's schema, 2026-11-14): a change is tested within its component (its in-app checks; the self-tests are chosen by what they compile, wherever they are), and `gate.py change --dependents` widens it to the components that depend on it; a change to shared code or to a contract runs every component's checks (cross-component); the whole suite runs nightly and at a release. A path (app-relative; `../../` is the repository's; a trailing / a folder, * a glob) is owned by the first entry that matches: contracts, shared, then the components in order. `gate.py self-test` holds that every source is owned, and that what each self-test compiles crosses only the `depends` declared here.",
 "contracts": {
  "why": "what two components agree on: a change here is cross-component",
  "paths": [
   "../../API-SPEC-*",
   "../../CONTRACT-*",
   "../../engine/include/",
   "../../engine/src/core/params.*",
   "../../engine/src/pipeline/engine.cpp",
